1
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:12,920
Just know it lightly and try stepping away.

2
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:28,600
Like someone is calling you,
an afternoon after the rain.

3
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:35,300
Walking while looking back,
holding Gaa-chan's hand.

4
00:00:36,180 --> 00:00:42,420
That strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:47,700
So, on the arcade's guide tiles,

6
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,500
I tried walking only on the black ones.

7
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,660
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,800
but everyone has forgotten.

9
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:09,080
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

10
00:01:09,540 --> 00:01:14,660
Try turning at that corner.

11
00:01:15,620 --> 00:01:19,880
You can meet everyone, everyone.

12
00:01:22,020 --> 00:01:27,780
Over there is Kame-ari surely Kame-ari.

13
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:33,080
Everyone, come on over to our town!

14
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:34,560
Thank you.

15
00:01:38,340 --> 00:01:41,420
Dad, that place over there is glowing.
What is it?

16
00:01:41,420 --> 00:01:46,360
That's Tokyo Stadium,
a brand-new baseball park.

17
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:52,360
The lights of Tokyo Stadium
were easy to see from the train.

18
00:01:53,740 --> 00:01:58,000
In June, Showa 37
(1962), as the home stadium of the Daimai Orions,

19
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,620
Tokyo Stadium was built in Minami-Senju,
Arakawa Ward.

20
00:02:02,060 --> 00:02:07,200
It was a huge ballpark with a total construction
cost of 3 billion yen and a capacity of 35,000 people.

21
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:10,720
The lighting, called
"candlesticks" like those in America's major leagues,

22
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:14,520
blazed intensely bright in the old downtown area,
where there were few buildings.

23
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:18,060
It was truly a stadium of light.

24
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:31,820
This is a light from the
floodlight of that Tokyo Stadium.

25
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:35,960
But why do you have
something like that, Senpai?

26
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:40,820
Tokyo Stadium holds
irreplaceable memories for me.

27
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:44,620
its history came to an
end after just ten years.

28
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:47,800
and when it was finally
going to be torn down,

29
00:02:51,460 --> 00:02:54,580
Hey! Miyoshi! It's dangerous!

30
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:55,860
Stop it!

31
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:58,760
Hey! Don't go! Get down!

32
00:02:59,740 --> 00:03:02,500
They're tearing it down anyway,
so one little piece is fine, right?

33
00:03:04,440 --> 00:03:05,240
Miyoshi!

34
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:09,420
You didn't cut the power?! Sorry!

35
00:03:13,940 --> 00:03:17,520
After all, it's from the light of that Tokyo Stadium,
the one with the lights.

36
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:19,840
It's sure to sell for a high price.

37
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:23,140
Sure, at today's baseball goods auction,

38
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:25,520
lots of collectors will be gathering.

39
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:27,640
It'll probably fetch a considerable price,

40
00:03:28,140 --> 00:03:29,580
but it's a keepsake, isn't it?

41
00:03:30,060 --> 00:03:31,160
You really intend to sell it?

42
00:03:31,700 --> 00:03:34,200
Memories of the past don't fill your belly.
Tomorrow's meal matters more.

43
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:38,420
Somehow it feels like time
hasn't been moving since earlier.

44
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:42,180
That clock has been stopped since we came in,
you know.

45
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:44,480
It's five minutes to ten now.

46
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:48,420
What? The auction starts at
ten and we're about to miss it!

47
00:03:48,940 --> 00:03:51,100
You idiot, at least set the clock!

48
00:03:51,540 --> 00:03:52,300
Senpai,

49
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:52,780
Ryo-chan,

50
00:03:52,780 --> 00:03:58,000
Ryo-chan,

51
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:00,540
are you all right?

52
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:03,520
The bulb is safe.

53
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:15,180
Who'd have thought the senior officer would
break a bone just from getting hit by a car!

54
00:04:15,180 --> 00:04:18,980
You tried to sell a cherished keepsake,
so you got punished for it.

55
00:04:18,980 --> 00:04:22,300
What I do with my own things is my business,
isn't it?

56
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:25,080
We won't make it to the auction now,
will we?

57
00:04:25,580 --> 00:04:29,920
Damn it,
there are still 29 days until next Friday!

58
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:32,880
I'm truly sorry.

59
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:34,640
I don't know how to apologize.

60
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:36,940
Exactly,
what are you going to do about this?

61
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:43,020
I'm sorry. We'll cover all the costs until your leg is fully healed,
so please let us take care of everything.

62
00:04:43,020 --> 00:04:44,040
Really?

63
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:47,100
Good for you,
no need to worry about meals anymore!

64
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:51,380
Have we met somewhere before?

65
00:04:51,860 --> 00:04:53,940
No, I believe this is our first time,
isn't it?

66
00:04:54,580 --> 00:04:55,380
I see.

67
00:04:57,200 --> 00:04:59,360
Is it true Ryo-san got hurt?

68
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:00,920
As you can see.

69
00:05:01,520 --> 00:05:03,720
What about today's game?

70
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:06,420
That's right,
it starts at three, doesn't it?

71
00:05:06,940 --> 00:05:11,300
What's happening today? It's the
neighborhood baseball game against the PTA.

72
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:17,480
I was supposed to play in place of these kids' parents,
but with that leg, there's no way.

73
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:21,340
Hey, you promised you'd hit a home run!

74
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:25,940
Don't worry, I'll keep my promise.

75
00:05:34,420 --> 00:05:35,380
Let's go.

76
00:05:36,420 --> 00:05:36,860
Here we go.

77
00:05:41,820 --> 00:05:43,440
Senpai!

78
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:46,040
Are you all right?

79
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:48,620
It's no use. Not on that leg.

80
00:05:48,620 --> 00:05:52,100
That's right.
These kids will understand too.

81
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:54,400
A man has to keep a
promise once he's made it.

82
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:58,240
Both your legs are broken, you know.

83
00:05:58,240 --> 00:05:59,280
So what? That's nothing.

84
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:03,120
I'm keeping my promise
to some damn cheeky brat.

85
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:06,880
I know a man who hit a home
run with a full-body fracture.

86
00:06:09,140 --> 00:06:10,480
That player's name was

87
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:12,960
Hyuga Kenji.

88
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:16,160
Hyuga Kenji?

89
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:17,040
I don't know him.

90
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:18,540
An old player?

91
00:06:19,340 --> 00:06:22,200
It's a story from long
before you two were born.

92
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:27,040
There was a professional baseball stadium here called Tokyo Stadium,
you see.

93
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:30,240
Hyuga was a player who was active here.

94
00:06:32,180 --> 00:06:36,680
So the Tokyo Stadium you were talking
about earlier was actually here?

95
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:41,300
Yeah. It was a stadium
that gave us so many dreams.

96
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:48,520
Dad, hurry up!

97
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:51,460
It's fine,
the night game goes on until nine.

98
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:54,320
Wow, it's so bright!

99
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:57,080
I wonder if everyone's gathered yet.

100
00:06:58,220 --> 00:07:00,280
Hey, Gin-san, you're early today!

101
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:02,060
Should we bet on this one?

102
00:07:05,780 --> 00:07:07,100
Two diamonds.

103
00:07:07,100 --> 00:07:08,180
Hurry, hurry!

104
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:16,040
Hey, Dad, which team is winning?

105
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:17,100
Hold on a second.

106
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:18,300
Let's see.

107
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:21,780
Alright, the pinch hitter's up first!

108
00:07:22,200 --> 00:07:22,660
Yay!

109
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:25,460
Hey, Asakusa old man, we saved you a seat!

110
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:26,980
Perfect timing!

111
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:28,840
Hose, the usual, please!

112
00:07:29,380 --> 00:07:30,660
Go, Kankichi!

113
00:07:30,840 --> 00:07:31,360
Yeah!

114
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,542
Fight, fight,

115
00:07:38,592 --> 00:07:40,860
Oo-mai, go!

116
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:44,720
Fight, fight, Oo-mai! Fight, fight, Oo-mai!

117
00:07:47,380 --> 00:07:50,240
Yes! The Missile lineup explodes!

118
00:07:52,200 --> 00:07:53,640
Way to go, Enomoto!

119
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:56,580
Way to go, way to go, Enomoto!

120
00:07:58,320 --> 00:08:01,720
Konis, the first-base side is really heating up now,
isn't it?

121
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:04,154
Well, how should I put it, Shimura-san,

122
00:08:04,204 --> 00:08:07,620
I'd say it's a hit pushed along by the cheering,
you could say.

123
00:08:08,300 --> 00:08:12,240
And now stepping up to the plate
is the young hero of the Orions.

124
00:08:12,840 --> 00:08:16,680
Cleanup, third base,
Hyuga, uniform number 0.

125
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:23,360
Hyuga Kenji was still barely
twenty years old back then,

126
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:27,300
but he was the slugger entrusted with
the cleanup spot in the Missile lineup.

127
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:30,520
Hit it out, Hyuga!

128
00:08:30,520 --> 00:08:32,480
Knock 'em down!

129
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:34,020
Here it goes!

130
00:08:34,660 --> 00:08:37,280
Hit it out, Hyuga!

131
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:39,200
Adachi on the mound!

132
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:42,700
From the set position,
the pitch in the ninth inning...

133
00:08:50,340 --> 00:08:53,900
It's in! No days off, a three-run home run!

134
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:55,140
Yay!

135
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:58,880
Banzai! Banzai!

136
00:08:58,880 --> 00:09:01,220
Banzai! Banzai!

137
00:09:01,220 --> 00:09:06,040
Thanks to Bōzu, we've added another run!
Here's Goby's yakisoba!

138
00:09:06,040 --> 00:09:09,800
Thanks! We've got cider too.
How about a PET bottle?

139
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:10,900
Yay!

140
00:09:13,020 --> 00:09:14,240
Thanks for always cheering us on.

141
00:09:17,280 --> 00:09:19,260
Hyuga-san just talked to me!

142
00:09:19,760 --> 00:09:21,760
Here, Kankichi, eat up!

143
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:23,920
Because that's your dinner, got it?

144
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:24,500
Mm-hmm.

145
00:09:28,540 --> 00:09:35,320
Damn, already switching sides?

146
00:09:35,720 --> 00:09:37,340
I'm going out for a bit in the meantime.

147
00:09:38,180 --> 00:09:41,940
Actually, I had another reason
for coming to Tokyo Stadium.

148
00:09:41,940 --> 00:09:45,940
No, this one was really the main purpose.

149
00:09:45,940 --> 00:09:47,860
Hey, are there any lost kids here?

150
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:50,480
Hey, lost kid!

151
00:09:52,560 --> 00:09:54,460
Found one, lucky!

152
00:09:56,640 --> 00:09:59,140
You kids are precious treasures.

153
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:00,720
Are there any others?

154
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:05,080
Top of the fifth, the Braves are at bat.

155
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:08,080
The batter is the sixth hitter,
at second base.

156
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:10,760
Barbon, number four.

157
00:10:13,760 --> 00:10:14,540
Miss

158
00:10:15,400 --> 00:10:16,560
Kankichi-kun

159
00:10:16,560 --> 00:10:19,200
Thanks for the baseball cards the other day.

160
00:10:20,500 --> 00:10:22,940
I happened to find another lost child.

161
00:10:24,020 --> 00:10:25,380
Thanks for your hard work, as always.

162
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:30,320
No, I'm happy if I can
be of help to you, Miss.

163
00:10:33,220 --> 00:10:35,060
We have a lost child announcement.

164
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:38,140
Mr. Yamada, visiting from Mikawajima.

165
00:10:38,140 --> 00:10:41,240
Your son, Taro,
has become separated from you.

166
00:10:41,940 --> 00:10:44,720
Please come to the office
under the stands immediately.

167
00:10:45,760 --> 00:10:47,520
What a pleasant voice to listen to.

168
00:10:47,940 --> 00:10:50,420
It's refreshing, isn't it, gentlemen?

169
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:51,920
Yes.

170
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:54,040
It's candy.

171
00:10:55,140 --> 00:10:56,660
No, it's fine.

172
00:10:57,540 --> 00:11:00,500
Wait quietly until your dad comes, okay?

173
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:01,740
Okay!

174
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:02,940
Yes.

175
00:11:05,920 --> 00:11:07,020
For Kankichi-kun, too.

176
00:11:08,600 --> 00:11:11,020
I love this rain too.

177
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:16,360
Her name was Yayoi Kurihara.

178
00:11:16,360 --> 00:11:19,540
She ran the Ugui Market stall at Tokyo Stadium,
you know.

179
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:23,840
Not only did she have a beautiful voice,
she was truly lovely and kind.

180
00:11:24,820 --> 00:11:28,760
I was practically going to
the ballpark just to see her.

181
00:11:30,220 --> 00:11:31,520
Sounds like something you'd do, Ryo-chan.

182
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:35,020
Once, I just couldn't find a lost child,

183
00:11:35,020 --> 00:11:38,820
so I dressed up my little brother
Kinjirō as one and took him there.

184
00:11:38,820 --> 00:11:41,160
Dad found out and gave me a solid beating.

185
00:11:41,940 --> 00:11:44,560
Hahaha, well, of course he did.

186
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:47,180
Hey, what happened to the home run story?

187
00:11:47,180 --> 00:11:49,580
Forget the woman stuff, already!

188
00:11:50,100 --> 00:11:53,780
Don't rush!
She's actually a big part of it too.

189
00:11:53,780 --> 00:11:56,280
That legendary home run, you see,

190
00:12:18,920 --> 00:12:21,440
Wow, Hyuga's autographed ball!

191
00:12:21,440 --> 00:12:25,540
Hyuga said,
"Thanks for always cheering for me,"

192
00:12:25,540 --> 00:12:28,700
Yes! I can brag about it
all over the neighborhood!

193
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:31,720
I thought I'd give it to you now,
while I have the chance.

194
00:12:32,380 --> 00:12:34,360
Yeah, it's almost time, isn't it.

195
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:35,700
What?

196
00:12:36,980 --> 00:12:40,780
Yayoi-san is quitting the Ugui
stall at the end of this season.

197
00:12:40,780 --> 00:12:42,640
Why?

198
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:45,040
Because she's getting married.

199
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:46,660
To who?

200
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:50,940
Hyuga?

201
00:12:55,480 --> 00:12:59,740
Cleanup hitter, third base,
Hyuga, number zero.

202
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:07,300
Sorry, Kankichi. I meant to tell you sooner.

203
00:13:16,020 --> 00:13:16,860
What is it?

204
00:13:16,860 --> 00:13:19,520
Damn it! What's so great about Hyuga?

205
00:13:24,020 --> 00:13:26,580
Yes! It's a comeback!

206
00:13:27,420 --> 00:13:28,740
Go for it, Hyuga!

207
00:13:29,860 --> 00:13:31,220
Not even a little bit good!

208
00:13:32,740 --> 00:13:33,915
Ever since that day,

209
00:13:33,965 --> 00:13:36,940
I stopped going to the ballpark.

210
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:44,800
Cleanup, third base, Hyuga!

211
00:13:44,800 --> 00:13:46,120
Number zero.

212
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,600
Hit one out, Hyuga!

213
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:49,480
It's a comeback!

214
00:13:55,580 --> 00:13:58,820
It's not as exciting
without that brat here, is it?

215
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:01,880
That kid hasn't been coming lately, has she?

216
00:14:01,880 --> 00:14:03,080
Yeah, she hasn't.

217
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:06,320
Looks like that girl liked you, you know.

218
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:09,980
I bet she was shocked when she found out.

219
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:22,260
What a disgrace. Ōmae's on an eight-game losing streak,
they say.

220
00:14:22,840 --> 00:14:25,900
Another hit this week How about that?

221
00:14:26,540 --> 00:14:32,960
I'm just going to go pump myself up a bit. If you want to go to Tokyo Stadium,
Dad's going alone.

222
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:36,220
Then go. I've decided I'm never going again.

223
00:14:37,520 --> 00:14:41,120
You were nagging me to take you every night until just recently,
you know.

224
00:14:41,980 --> 00:14:44,460
What's with Hyuga, anyway?

225
00:14:44,460 --> 00:14:50,780
I'd never cheer for him, not even if I died!
Excuse me!

226
00:14:52,520 --> 00:14:53,380
Eeeeeh!

227
00:14:56,740 --> 00:14:57,780
It's Hyuga!

228
00:14:57,780 --> 00:15:00,560
I told you I hate Hyuga!

229
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:03,240
That Hyuga is here at the shop!

230
00:15:06,700 --> 00:15:07,780
It's the real thing!

231
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:10,720
Hey, you're Kankichi, right?

232
00:15:10,720 --> 00:15:12,780
H-how do you know that?

233
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:16,160
Because you always cheer
for me from up on the bench.

234
00:15:16,620 --> 00:15:19,820
Plus, I've heard about you from Yayoi too.

235
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:20,320
Yeah.

236
00:15:21,820 --> 00:15:23,340
Do you have some time right now?

237
00:15:23,740 --> 00:15:25,320
Want to play catch?

238
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:33,700
You throw a pretty good ball, you know.

239
00:15:33,700 --> 00:15:34,980
You've got potential.

240
00:15:37,760 --> 00:15:40,440
I don't want to become a pro
baseball player or anything!

241
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:43,160
I hate pro baseball players.

242
00:15:56,940 --> 00:15:58,100
Take a look at that ball.

243
00:16:02,280 --> 00:16:04,180
Kankichi-kun, how have you been?

244
00:16:05,040 --> 00:16:07,380
I've missed seeing you lately.
It's been so lonely.

245
00:16:08,180 --> 00:16:10,260
Please show me your cheerful face again.

246
00:16:12,560 --> 00:16:16,680
Yayoi and I want you to bless our marriage.

247
00:16:17,400 --> 00:16:20,460
Would you give us your
approval for our marriage?

248
00:16:21,560 --> 00:16:23,940
I'll make her happy, I promise.

249
00:16:24,340 --> 00:16:25,620
Can you believe that?

250
00:16:26,740 --> 00:16:30,740
A great no-hitter, sure, but if you don't hit,
you'll get cut from the pros, right?

251
00:16:31,180 --> 00:16:34,420
How do you expect to make your
big sister happy with that attitude!

252
00:16:37,020 --> 00:16:39,100
Got it! Then I'll hit one!

253
00:16:41,420 --> 00:16:42,298
Two weeks later,

254
00:16:42,348 --> 00:16:46,620
the season's final game will
be played at Tokyo Stadium.

255
00:16:47,320 --> 00:16:49,540
It's also Yayoi's last game.

256
00:16:50,840 --> 00:16:52,900
I'll hit a home run in that game!

257
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:55,520
R-really? You promise?

258
00:16:56,820 --> 00:16:57,580
I promise!

259
00:16:58,280 --> 00:17:00,540
You promise, promise, promise?

260
00:17:01,320 --> 00:17:03,280
I promise, promise, promise!

261
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:05,480
It's a promise between men!

262
00:17:06,980 --> 00:17:09,120
Yeah, a promise between men!

263
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:14,180
Kankichi-kun?

264
00:17:14,680 --> 00:17:16,400
Something got in my eye!

265
00:17:17,300 --> 00:17:20,380
You'd better hit it, or I won't forgive you!

266
00:17:34,940 --> 00:17:36,520
It was a serious injury, two months long.

267
00:17:38,980 --> 00:17:40,440
What are we doing, Kankichi?

268
00:17:40,860 --> 00:17:42,720
Today's the last game of the year, right?

269
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:44,540
Are we going or not?

270
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:45,760
Yeah.

271
00:17:46,340 --> 00:17:49,080
Go on ahead. I've got a stop to make first.

272
00:17:52,600 --> 00:17:54,460
Okay? Just five minutes.

273
00:17:54,900 --> 00:17:57,300
Hyuga's still not well, you know.

274
00:17:57,300 --> 00:17:57,600
Yeah.

275
00:17:59,540 --> 00:18:00,700
Hyuga!

276
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:02,020
N-no way.

277
00:18:04,420 --> 00:18:07,800
Now it's the bottom of the ninth,
and things have become unbelievable.

278
00:18:08,340 --> 00:18:09,720
Two outs, but the bases are loaded.

279
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:11,100
We're down by three runs.

280
00:18:11,100 --> 00:18:13,540
One hit and it's a walk-off comeback.

281
00:18:13,900 --> 00:18:16,700
Hyuga can end this season with a win.

282
00:18:17,240 --> 00:18:19,080
But the batting order is the worst.

283
00:18:19,080 --> 00:18:21,240
The next batter is pitcher Sakai.

284
00:18:22,020 --> 00:18:24,320
If only Hyuga were here at a time like this.

285
00:18:24,860 --> 00:18:27,740
Damn, we've cornered them this far,
and yet...

286
00:18:28,520 --> 00:18:29,000
Manager.

287
00:18:32,160 --> 00:18:34,280
Please, use me. Use me.

288
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:35,060
Hyuga!

289
00:18:35,240 --> 00:18:37,460
B-but you... your body...

290
00:18:37,900 --> 00:18:39,500
With Daida, I'll be fine.

291
00:18:41,220 --> 00:18:42,040
Please, Manager.

292
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:44,640
Understood.

293
00:18:45,580 --> 00:18:46,780
Daida Here we go.

294
00:18:47,100 --> 00:18:50,440
But didn't we already use up all our bench players,
like Yashu?

295
00:18:51,040 --> 00:18:52,060
Batter, substitution!

296
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:53,200
Yes.

297
00:18:56,720 --> 00:19:00,500
Batting for the Daimai Orions,
replacing Sakai,

298
00:19:02,060 --> 00:19:04,280
Hyuga, number zero.

299
00:19:05,020 --> 00:19:07,180
Well, this is certainly surprising.

300
00:19:07,180 --> 00:19:11,000
Who would have thought Hyuga, who should be in the hospital,
would show up at a moment like this.

301
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:15,480
How shall I put it?
You could call it a miraculous recovery.

302
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:19,440
But the opposing pitcher was hastily
brought in partway through the ninth inning.

303
00:19:19,440 --> 00:19:21,680
The formidable ace, Stancar.

304
00:19:22,040 --> 00:19:24,600
Can Hyuga, just back from his illness,
break through?

305
00:19:24,600 --> 00:19:25,820
Play!

306
00:19:25,820 --> 00:19:28,800
Stancar, from the set position,
throws the ninth pitch.

307
00:19:28,800 --> 00:19:31,700
He throws!

308
00:19:33,740 --> 00:19:35,040
Strike!

309
00:19:35,040 --> 00:19:36,760
Right down the middle.

310
00:19:36,760 --> 00:19:38,280
Hyuga can't lay a bat on it.

311
00:19:41,800 --> 00:19:43,660
It all comes down to one pitch

312
00:19:44,740 --> 00:19:46,020
Looks like it's no good after all.

313
00:19:46,020 --> 00:19:47,900
He's only just recovered from being sick,
after all.

314
00:19:49,300 --> 00:19:50,060
Everyone!

315
00:19:51,460 --> 00:19:52,400
Kankichi!

316
00:19:53,300 --> 00:19:57,800
Hyuga is standing at the plate,
enduring pain all over his body.

317
00:19:57,800 --> 00:20:01,400
If we don't cheer for him now, when will we?

318
00:20:02,720 --> 00:20:03,760
Here we go!

319
00:20:03,940 --> 00:20:07,260
Go, go, Hyuga!

320
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:09,620
Hit it out!

321
00:20:10,280 --> 00:20:11,020
Hit it!

322
00:20:11,780 --> 00:20:14,340
Fight fight, Hyuga!

323
00:20:14,400 --> 00:20:16,360
Knock it out!

324
00:20:21,620 --> 00:20:23,000
Kankichi-kun!

325
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:26,220
Hit it out! Hit it out!

326
00:20:26,380 --> 00:20:27,880
Hyuga!

327
00:20:28,520 --> 00:20:30,780
The stands are roaring with cheers.

328
00:20:33,020 --> 00:20:33,360
Hyuga!

329
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,300
Stancar throws the second pitch!

330
00:20:40,720 --> 00:20:41,880
For Yayoi-san,

331
00:20:44,620 --> 00:20:45,960
for Kankichi-kun,

332
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:49,500
I'll hit it for sure!

333
00:21:03,740 --> 00:21:04,520
Yahoo!

334
00:21:05,020 --> 00:21:06,900
Ryotsu and Hyuga!

335
00:21:07,020 --> 00:21:08,380
Big hit! Comeback!

336
00:21:08,460 --> 00:21:09,560
Grand slam!

337
00:21:09,860 --> 00:21:11,200
We did it!

338
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:12,900
Over there too.

339
00:21:13,420 --> 00:21:15,380
Look, you too.

340
00:21:15,380 --> 00:21:17,880
W-wow, it's amazing, it's amazing.

341
00:21:17,880 --> 00:21:20,120
I've never seen such an amazing home run.

342
00:21:21,040 --> 00:21:23,180
Because it was a promise between men.

343
00:21:23,540 --> 00:21:23,860
Yeah.

344
00:21:26,240 --> 00:21:27,200
Big sis.

345
00:21:27,900 --> 00:21:28,660
Yayoi-san.

346
00:21:28,660 --> 00:21:30,040
Kenji-san.

347
00:21:33,440 --> 00:21:34,160
Thank you, thank you!

348
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:36,760
You're the best, Mr. Hyuga!

349
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:38,140
Yahoo!

350
00:21:38,620 --> 00:21:40,560
Estimated distance: 200 meters.

351
00:21:40,560 --> 00:21:43,220
Hyuga's home run became a legend.

352
00:21:43,840 --> 00:21:45,680
He really was an amazing guy.

353
00:21:46,320 --> 00:21:47,840
Your father, you know,

354
00:21:47,840 --> 00:21:49,360
Hyuga Kenichi.

355
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:52,840
How do you know my name?

356
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:55,840
I had a feeling the first time we met.

357
00:21:56,300 --> 00:21:59,320
Because he looked just like
Hyuga Kenji when he was young.

358
00:22:00,040 --> 00:22:03,080
Or was he one of the top sluggers
in university baseball, right?

359
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:07,000
So are you going pro? Like your dad?

360
00:22:07,840 --> 00:22:11,100
Well, a few teams have approached me,
that's true.

361
00:22:12,160 --> 00:22:16,920
But I don't have the confidence to
become a legendary batter like my dad.

362
00:22:16,920 --> 00:22:18,060
Idiot!

363
00:22:19,740 --> 00:22:23,600
Your dad isn't great
because he made a legend.

364
00:22:23,600 --> 00:22:27,380
It's because he stepped up to the plate with
his life on the line to fulfill his duty.

365
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:31,280
Just to keep his promise to that kid.

366
00:22:32,160 --> 00:22:33,120
Legends are...

367
00:22:33,120 --> 00:22:37,060
aren't they simply the result
of giving your all to something?

368
00:22:39,800 --> 00:22:40,860
Hey, Ryo-san.

369
00:22:42,080 --> 00:22:43,180
Everyone's here.

370
00:22:43,180 --> 00:22:45,040
Alright, the game's starting.

371
00:22:45,860 --> 00:22:46,440
Ryo-chan.

372
00:22:47,920 --> 00:22:51,460
Ryo-san, please put me in for this game.

373
00:22:52,740 --> 00:22:55,280
I'll definitely hit a home run.

374
00:22:57,040 --> 00:22:58,460
Alright, it's a promise.

375
00:22:58,460 --> 00:22:59,880
Not just me,

376
00:22:59,880 --> 00:23:01,480
Junpei and Kappei,

377
00:23:01,480 --> 00:23:03,960
and with Nakagawa, Reiko,
and the others, too.

378
00:23:04,620 --> 00:23:05,020
Yes.

379
00:23:18,220 --> 00:23:19,420
Hit a home run.

380
00:23:19,880 --> 00:23:21,040
Promise?

381
00:23:27,560 --> 00:23:28,280
Alright!

382
00:23:28,280 --> 00:23:28,980
Amazing.

383
00:23:28,980 --> 00:23:31,700
Just as expected of the
university's top swagger.

384
00:23:31,700 --> 00:23:32,560
Yay!

385
00:23:35,340 --> 00:23:37,400
I'll give this to him.

386
00:23:37,860 --> 00:23:40,600
He's the most worthy of owning it.

387
00:23:41,580 --> 00:23:44,780
And my most precious treasure is...

388
00:23:45,260 --> 00:23:47,220
I've been keeping it safe, after all.

389
00:24:07,300 --> 00:24:13,920
First I draw my eyebrows,
then dash, dash, dash to the station!

390
00:24:13,920 --> 00:24:19,500
Packed train, a quick nap on the way home.

391
00:24:20,560 --> 00:24:25,820
Another tough week, so much hard work,
and yes, you're absolutely right.

392
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:30,560
But I'm getting by with just one hand,

393
00:24:30,560 --> 00:24:33,260
beef bowl with extra sauce,
cloudy and dripping.

394
00:24:33,260 --> 00:24:36,560
Overtime after overtime, all the irritation,

395
00:24:36,560 --> 00:24:40,200
ylang-ylang clears it right up.

396
00:24:43,580 --> 00:24:46,340
Every day is no problem.

397
00:24:46,340 --> 00:24:50,000
After a dip under the hot shower,

398
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:53,000
every day is no problem.

399
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:56,600
My sleep pillow restores my energy.

400
00:24:59,760 --> 00:25:02,520
Every day is no problem

401
00:25:03,540 --> 00:25:06,180
I love a girl like me

402
00:25:06,180 --> 00:25:09,380
Every day is no brain

403
00:25:09,380 --> 00:25:13,020
Monday with hearts flying around

404
00:25:13,440 --> 00:25:17,500
Manday, Manday, no problem brain

405
00:25:20,600 --> 00:25:24,260
You're going to the Shitaya Daiko
police box in Ueno as a backup?

406
00:25:24,500 --> 00:25:25,600
Leave it to me.

407
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:28,080
That area's my home turf, you know.

408
00:25:28,640 --> 00:25:30,260
What is this police box?

409
00:25:30,260 --> 00:25:31,820
Aside from dogs and cats,

410
00:25:34,460 --> 00:25:37,720
Next time, it's Hitomachi Police Box Diary.
See you then!

